设计定稿：

```js
/**
 * token-budget — a per-session token budget gate, the dsh-side counterpart of the
 * `usage_limited` / `budget_limited` statuses in Codex's thread_goals table.
 *
 * WHY: dsh's goal row carries an objective but no cost ceiling, and the user's own
 * usage log shows a single session reaching 490M tokens. Codex models this in the
 * goal status enum; here it is a separate, observable gate.
 *
 * SOURCE OF TRUTH: provider-reported usage on each `assistant/message` event
 * (`data.usage` = inputTokens / outputTokens / cacheReadTokens), the same samples
 * @deepseek-ai/dsh-token-meter folds into its `tokenUsage` projection. No estimation.
 *
 * BEHAVIOR: counts usage per session; when the effective budget is crossed it injects
 * ONE short next-step note (never a block — the model decides how to wrap up).
 */
```

